+  // comb's rings hold of it, the way the classic filter does it: brightness through the notch (which the
+  // adaptive comb falls back to there anyway), colour straight from the signal, not faded. Only the picture's
+  // own stretch of that one line is replaced and nothing in push() changes: levels, burst and every other line
+  // come out exactly as they did.
